    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0345" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1186.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Henry to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Puerto Plata</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-29T12:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1914, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had an interview with Bordas this morning. He declares that Puerto Plata is
                    blockaded, he will continue to use cannon against the town but promises care. Do
                    not believe Government has much more than thousand soldiers Cibao and four
                    hundred attacking here. The situation unchanged. Gunboat is essential for the
                    protection of foreigners. English have requested one.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
